    "answer": {
      "short": "$9818$.\n\nCount in base six, then replace digits $0,1,2,3,4,5$ by $0,1,4,6,8,9$ respectively.",
      "worked": "The prime digits are $2,3,5,7$, so the permitted digits are $0,1,4,6,8,9$. These six digits correspond, in order, to the base-six digits $0,1,2,3,4,5$. This correspondence preserves increasing order and sends the first positive base-six integer to the first prime-free number.\n\nConvert the position to base six:\n$$\\begin{align*}1234&=5\\times6^3+4\\times6^2+1\\times6+4\\\\1234&=5414_6.\\end{align*}$$\nReplace each base-six digit using $0\\mapsto0$, $1\\mapsto1$, $2\\mapsto4$, $3\\mapsto6$, $4\\mapsto8$, $5\\mapsto9$. Thus $5414_6$ corresponds to $9818$, the $1234^{\\text{th}}$ prime-free number.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
